<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratan Singh of Ratlam</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1618–1658</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratan Singh was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathore</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a>, a descendant of Raja <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udai-singh-of-marwar">Udai Singh of Marwar</a>, who received Ratlam in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a> from the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shah-jahan">Shah Jahan</a> in 1652 in reward for service. He founded the Ratlam state and was killed at the Battle of Dharmat in 1658, fighting in the imperial army against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>.</p></div>
